only the HTML is. See kernel/SOURCE.pin.)

This REPLACES the v3 we carried (1, 2, 4-7 of 8), itself the replacement for
0515/0516/0517 (v2 1-3 of 6). Of the ten in v4 we take 1-3 and 5-9, and skip:
  4/10   flush the MDP5 interface before starting the timing engine -- MDP5
         only (db820c); every SoC we ship has a DPU.
  10/10  drm/ci xfail bookkeeping for SC7180.
v4 says it now DEPENDS on a separate series, "drm/msm: KMS destroy fixes"
<20261003-msm-kms-destroy-fixes-v1-*>, which is where v3's 3/8 (unwind
msm_drm_kms_init() on failure) went. We did not carry v3's 3/8 either: those
are init/teardown error-path fixes, and the eight here apply on top of our
stack at fuzz 0 and build without them.

WHAT CHANGED FROM THE v3 WE CARRIED:
  - 1: the pin lock is taken with guard() instead of unwinding through labels
    (Rob). Same semantics.
  - 3: a RACE FIX, not a cleanup. v3 scheduled the retired framebuffer's
    vblank work and added it to the crtc's pending list separately, so
    msm_crtc_vblank_off() could free it in between; v4 does both under one
    lock. v3 also decided "vblank is off" from crtc->state, which a following
    commit may already have swapped; v4 tracks it next to the list.
  - 4, 5 (CWB, CDM) are NEW: the same bug class as the DSPP and DSC fixes,
    pointers from a previous reservation surviving into one which no longer
    owns those blocks.

7/8 OF v3 (NOW 9/10) WAS SKIPPED ON 2026-09-12 AND THAT DECISION WAS
REVERSED -- read this before ever dropping it again. The skip reasoning was:
it gates on CRTC colour management, gamescope 3.16.28 writes 0 to CTM,
GAMMA_LUT and DEGAMMA_LUT on every path and does colour in its own Vulkan
composite instead, so crtc_state->ctm is never non-NULL for us and both the
hack it deletes and the modeset it adds are dead code. That was correct at the
time and is now obsolete: DPU inline rotation (0340) means gamescope takes
DIRECT SCANOUT, where its Vulkan composite -- and therefore ALL of its colour
management -- never runs. CONFIRMED ON HARDWARE 2026-09-13 on Pocket FIT: night
mode forced to maximum via the GAMESCOPE_COLOR_NIGHT_MODE atom is completely
invisible, and the amber appears the instant GAMESCOPE_COMPOSITE_FORCE=1 is
set. The fix is to drive the DPU's DSPP CTM + GAMMA_LUT from gamescope and keep
scanout, so crtc_state->ctm becomes non-NULL in normal operation -- which is
exactly the configuration 9/10 fixes, and whose upstream reproducer
(kms_plane@pixel-format-source-clamping) is a CTM test. Without 9/10 the first
CTM would re-reserve resources without reprogramming the encoder, CTL_FLUSH
would be written with zero, and the display would freeze with the pipe still
fetching. 6 below (the DSPP pointer) stops being theoretical for the same
reason.

WHY WE CARE, per patch (numbered as in the list above):
  1  The race needs commit N+1's ->prepare_fb() to overlap commit N's
     ->cleanup_fb() on the same buffer, which is gamescope's steady state:
     nonblocking atomic commits over a double-buffered flip.
  2  Rarer trigger -- it needs a prepare to fail first -- but a worse outcome:
     the count sticks, so from then on every prepare of that framebuffer
     reports success while iova[] is still zero. Permanent, not transient.
  3  The reason we took the series at all. Every panel driver we ship except
     the two ICNA35XX-family ones sets MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO, so this is the
     configuration nearly the whole fleet runs in. Same failure class as
     0370-dpu-quiesce-boot-scanout.patch, which covers the boot handover; this
     covers the runtime teardowns. The v4 lock fix matters on every display
     disable, i.e. every suspend.
  4  CWB is concurrent writeback, which nothing here requests. NULL-safety,
     taken because it is cheap and the series moves as a unit.
  5  CDM is reserved for YUV writeback and DP. Same reasoning as 4.
  6  Two lines. It could not fire while nothing requested a DSPP, which was
     true until we decided to drive the DPU's colour blocks; once gamescope
     sets a CTM, topologies really do gain and lose DSPPs and this becomes a
     live fix rather than NULL-safety. See the 9/10 note above.
  7  Pocket FIT's panel is DSC-only with slice_width 540 on a 1080-wide panel,
     ie. slice_count 2, so its encoder really does drive two DSC blocks.
     Cheap insurance against a false DSC-merge after a topology change.
  8  The prerequisite for doing colour management in the DPU at all. Note what
     it means for userspace: enabling colour management now REQUIRES a commit
     with DRM_MODE_ATOMIC_ALLOW_MODESET, because the kernel no longer forces
     allow_modeset on our behalf. gamescope's per-frame flips are nonblocking
     and non-allow-modeset, so the plan is to establish an identity CTM at
     modeset time -- keeping DSPPs in the topology for the life of the mode --
     and then update the CTM blob per frame, which needs no further modeset.

